```

Requirement: delete the early Replace. Meta?.LeaveMatch is the only intent, page stays until unified recovery completes. Also "房间页可点离房按钮时必要禁用防重复，但不能无Meta配置时永久禁". Minimal delete Replace is enough; flow idempotent handles duplicates. So should I add disable? "可点离房按钮时必要禁用防重复，但不能无Meta配置时永久禁；最小删除Replace足够，flow幂等处理重复。" This means minimal delete of Replace is enough; no need to add disabling. But we need to also remove unused `using`? Replace likely comes from base, PageIds might not be used elsewhere in the file. Let's check: PageIds appears only line 68. After deleting, is `LiteFramework.UI` still needed? Yes for PageLogicBase etc. PageIds may be from LiteGame namespace or LiteFramework.UI. No using removal needed since UI is used. But the using System.Collections.Generic is used.

Update comment on the method to current conclusion ≤ budget. Comment: e.g. `/// <summary>离房：只表达离房意图，页面保留到统一恢复完成后再回大厅。</summary>` ≤4 lines. Good.

Do we need a disable? "房间页可点离房按钮时必要禁用防重复" — Hmm reads as "when the leave button can be clicked, disable as necessary to prevent duplicates, but must not permanently disable when Meta is not configured". This suggests adding defensive disabling. But "最小删除Replace足够，flow幂等处理重复" says minimal delete Replace suffices, flow idempotency handles duplicate. So don't add _leaving gating in room page. Keep minimal. Perhaps just delete Replace and update comment.

Settings page: ConfirmExitAsync:
```csharp
if (_leaving) return;
_leaving = true;
SetInteractable("Btn_ExitMatch", false);
IConfirmDialog confirm = Ctx?.Confirm;
if (confirm == null) { _leaving = false; SetInteractable(...true); return; }
int generation = Form.DisplayGeneration;
bool ok = await confirm.ShowAsync(...);
_leaving = false;
if (!Form.IsDisplayCurrent(generation)) return;
SetInteractable("Btn_ExitMatch", true);
if (!ok) return;
Replace(PageIds.Page_Lobby);  // 先回大厅...
Meta?.LeaveMatch();
```

Requirement: "_leaving=false先generation检查是同型旧回调问题，可将状态写移到generation校验后（只本方法）". So move `_leaving = false` to after the generation check (and before/after SetInteractable?). Need to think: if display stale, we return without resetting _leaving — but page hidden, OnPageHide resets _leaving. Hmm, but the method returns and _leaving stays true; OnPageHide sets _leaving=false. That's fine since page hidden. However if display is stale but page still shown? DisplayGeneration changes when form display regenerated; old callback should abandon. Requirement explicitly: "可将状态写移到generation校验后". So:

```csharp
int generation = Form.DisplayGeneration;
bool ok = await confirm.ShowAsync(...);
if (!Form.IsDisplayCurrent(generation)) return;
_leaving = false;
SetInteractable("Btn_ExitMatch", true);
if (!ok) return;
Meta?.LeaveMatch();
```

And remove Replace line. The SetInteractable true needed? Yes keep. But about duplicates: after confirm ok, button re-enabled, duplicates possible? Flow idempotent; user only asked delete Replace. Could keep button disabled while leaving? Minimal change as instructed. Keep.

Method comment update ≤ budget. Add XML summary e.g. `/// <summary>确认离房：只表达离房意图，页面保留到统一恢复完成；显示代次失效的旧回调直接放弃。</summary>` That's 1 line.

For Room Leave method, currently no comment. Add one.

Room page also has class summary line 6 mentioning "离房回大厅" — that's still conceptually true (recovery returns lobby), so leave. Don't over-edit.

Now check PageIds usage in Settings file: only line 289. Removing it leaves no reference to PageIds. Fine, no using needed.

But wait—`Replace` may still be used for other navigation? No.

Need to check whether `Meta?.LeaveMatch()` exists and page leave flows. Not necessary per user.

